# Optional environment for home-warden-catalog-heal.service / scripts/catalog-heal.
# Copy to ~/.config/home-warden-catalog-heal.env and chmod 600.
#
# External-DNS drift *detection/alerting* needs only Cloudflare credentials
# (conf/cloudflare.ini) and runs regardless of this setting. This target is
# needed only to *repair* a flagged record, and only once an operator runs
# `catalog-heal --apply-cert --apply-dns` by hand -- the timer never passes
# --apply-dns. Leaving this unset does not silence DNS alerts, it just
# means the eventual --apply-dns run will fail with "no dns_target
# configured" until it's set:
# DNS_SYNC_TARGET=203.0.113.10

# Required to receive mail instead of a log-only alert line (also needs the
# operator-saved [smtp] config -- see the web UI's Settings page):
# CATALOG_HEAL_ALERT_TO=you@example.com

# Overrides (defaults shown):
# CATALOG_HEAL_COOLDOWN_SEC=3600
# CATALOG_HEAL_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
# CATALOG_HEAL_WINDOW_SEC=86400
# CATALOG_HEAL_RESEND_SEC=21600
# ALERT_DAYS=10
# Leave SCRATCH_DIR unset to keep the unit default from setup-service.
# If overriding, use an absolute path (EnvironmentFile does not expand $HOME/%h):
# SCRATCH_DIR=/home/you/scratch/home-warden
